From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Subject: [PATCH] AP: ignore a Deauth/Disassoc TX status after its callback
 ended

WLAN_STA_PENDING_DEAUTH_CB and WLAN_STA_PENDING_DISASSOC_CB mark the
callback that the TX status of a Deauthentication or Disassociation
frame runs. Only ap_sta_deauth_cb() and ap_sta_disassoc_cb() clear
them, so the flag stays set where the two second timeout runs the
callback first, or where ap_sta_clear_disconnect_timeouts() cancels it
for a new authentication or association. A later TX status of the
frame, for example from a driver that holds the frame for a STA in
power save until the removal flushes it, then runs the callback again.
It removes the STA from the driver a second time, or removes the new
association of a STA that came back within the wait.

Clear the flag where the callback runs, from the TX status or from the
timeout, and where ap_sta_clear_disconnect_timeouts() cancels it. A
later TX status of the frame is then ignored, as that of a test frame
is.

Fixes: 4dc03726de07 ("Delay STA entry removal until Deauth/Disassoc TX status in AP mode")
Fixes: cc28ad8cdf38 ("Fix Deauth/Disassoc callback handling with test frames")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -1275,6 +1275,7 @@ static void ap_sta_disassoc_cb_timeout(void *eloop_ctx, void *timeout_ctx)
 
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "%s: Disassociation callback for STA " MACSTR,
 		   hapd->conf->iface, MAC2STR(sta->addr));
+	sta->flags &= ~WLAN_STA_PENDING_DISASSOC_CB;
 	ap_sta_remove(hapd, sta);
 	mlme_disassociate_indication(hapd, sta, sta->disassoc_reason);
 }
@@ -1357,6 +1358,7 @@ static void ap_sta_deauth_cb_timeout(void *eloop_ctx, void *timeout_ctx)
 
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "%s: Deauthentication callback for STA " MACSTR,
 		   hapd->conf->iface, MAC2STR(sta->addr));
+	sta->flags &= ~WLAN_STA_PENDING_DEAUTH_CB;
 	ap_sta_remove(hapd, sta);
 	mlme_deauthenticate_indication(hapd, sta, sta->deauth_reason);
 }
@@ -2245,7 +2247,6 @@ void ap_sta_deauth_cb(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta)
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "Ignore deauth cb for test frame");
 		return;
 	}
-	sta->flags &= ~WLAN_STA_PENDING_DEAUTH_CB;
 	eloop_cancel_timeout(ap_sta_deauth_cb_timeout, hapd, sta);
 	ap_sta_deauth_cb_timeout(hapd, sta);
 }
@@ -2257,7 +2258,6 @@ void ap_sta_disassoc_cb(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta)
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "Ignore disassoc cb for test frame");
 		return;
 	}
-	sta->flags &= ~WLAN_STA_PENDING_DISASSOC_CB;
 	eloop_cancel_timeout(ap_sta_disassoc_cb_timeout, hapd, sta);
 	ap_sta_disassoc_cb_timeout(hapd, sta);
 }
@@ -2276,6 +2276,8 @@ void ap_sta_clear_disconnect_timeouts(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 			   "%s: Removed ap_sta_disassoc_cb_timeout timeout for "
 			   MACSTR,
 			   hapd->conf->iface, MAC2STR(sta->addr));
+	sta->flags &= ~(WLAN_STA_PENDING_DEAUTH_CB |
+			WLAN_STA_PENDING_DISASSOC_CB);
 	if (eloop_cancel_timeout(ap_sta_delayed_1x_auth_fail_cb, hapd, sta) > 0)
 	{
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
